   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to certain funds used by the center for advanced technology",
    "basePrintNo": "S6854",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6854-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 3,
       "fullName": "Brian X. Foley",
       "imgName": "Brian X. Foley.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 448,
       "sessionMemberId": 34,
       "sessionYear": 2009,
       "shortName": "FOLEY"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3102-b, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6854\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to certain\nfunds used by the center for advanced technology\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo add elements to the enabling legislation that allow the centers to\noperate more efficiently and effectively\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nThe legislation would require the centers to accelerate technology\ndevelopment and commercialization, to facilitate new company\nformation, to conduct outreach to companies, and to provide evidence\nof partnerships with entities that aid in the economic development\ngrowth of the State; allow the matching requirement to be an overall\nmatch and not on a project-by-project basis, and allow matches from\nsmall businesses to count as double the actual dollar amount toward\nthe center's overall match requirement; extend the time period for\nquantifiable economic development impact measures to not less than\nfive years and require that the centers provide a full description of\nall non-quantifiable measures,\"\n\n EFFECTS OF PRESENT LAW WHICH THIS BILL WOULD ALTER :\n\nAdds to section 3102-b of public authorities law that authorized the\ncenters for advanced technology.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nMany procedural requirements for the operation of the centers are\ncarried on a contract-by-contract basis with the State and some of\nthese contract elements hinder the work that the centers can do This\nlegislation responds to the centers' unified requests for relief from\nthese restrictions, such as the way the match is determined, while\nmaintaining accountability and oversight\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
